---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "DTI for Self-Employed Income";
const description =
  "How self-employed income is used in DTI calculations, including net income, add-backs, and documentation basics. Educational use only.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/dti-self-employed-income">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Self-employed DTI</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>DTI for self-employed income</h1>
    <p>
      Self-employed income is usually based on net income, not gross receipts. This guide explains how to estimate a stable monthly
      income and what to document before running a DTI scenario.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/debt-to-income">DTI topic hub</a>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">DTI calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/dti-income-documentation-checklist">Income documentation</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Start with net income</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Many lenders use net income after expenses, which is why your gross receipts can look much higher than the income used in DTI.
      Use recent tax returns and year-to-date P&L statements to estimate a monthly net figure.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Typical documents</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Two years of business and personal tax returns.</li>
      <li>Year-to-date profit and loss statement.</li>
      <li>Balance sheet if required by the lender.</li>
      <li>Notes on any one-time expenses or add-backs.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Add-backs and adjustments</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        Some non-cash expenses may be added back by the lender. Only use add-backs that are allowed and documented; otherwise keep
        the estimate conservative.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Seasonal or volatile income</h2>
      <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
        If business income swings, average across a longer period to avoid overstating your monthly income. This keeps the DTI estimate
        aligned with underwriting reality.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common pitfalls</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Using gross revenue instead of net income.</li>
      <li>Counting income that is not documented.</li>
      <li>Ignoring recent declines in business income.</li>
      <li>Mixing personal and business debt payments.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Stability checks</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Compare year-over-year net income trends.</li>
      <li>Identify one-time expenses and document add-backs.</li>
      <li>Use conservative averages if income is declining.</li>
      <li>Keep business and personal cash flows separate.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/debt-to-income-calculator">Run DTI with net income</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/dti-variable-income-averaging">Variable income averaging</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/how-to-improve-dti">Improve DTI</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-31</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
